# An independent set of size 11466 in `C21^(box 4)`

`Jraw` lists 11466 codes of `C21^4`, encoded as in `BaseC21Data`: the union of the 26
cosets of `<(1,0,0,2),(0,1,2,0)> <= (ZZ/21)^4` given by a 26-point quotient code `Q`, namely
`(u, v, 2v+y, 2u+z)` for `(y,z) in Q` and `u,v in ZZ/21`.  Its size is 11466 = 26 * 21^2.

Membership is stored word-chunked in `maskW`, an array of 3039 64-bit words: a lookup
`(maskW[u / 64] >>> (u % 64)) &&& 1` reads a single word.
